   "
# ${agent.name} - Implementation

## Mission
Implement ${PROJECT_NAME} tasks T${agent.tasks.start}-T${agent.tasks.end} following orchestration strategy.

## Context Files
- Constitution: .specify/memory/constitution.md
- Spec: specs/001-mvp/spec.md
- Tasks: specs/001-mvp/tasks.md (focus on T${agent.tasks.start}-T${agent.tasks.end})
- Plan: specs/001-mvp/plan.md
- Design: design/design-tokens.json
- Memory: project-memory.md
- Orchestration: ORCHESTRATION.md (YOUR SECTION: ${agent.name})

## Filesystem Périmètres
**ALLOWED:**
${agent.allowed.map(d => `- ${d}`).join('\n')}

**FORBIDDEN:**
${agent.forbidden.map(d => `- ${d}`).join('\n')}

**Violation Handling:** STOP immediately + request coordination if you need to touch forbidden files.

## MCP Tools Allowed
${agent.tools.map(t => `- ${t}`).join('\n')}

## Quality Gates (MANDATORY)

**Every 10 tasks completed:**

1. **Gate P0: Build Check (BLOCKER)**
   \`\`\`bash
   pnpm build
   # Exit 1 if fails (STOP implementation)
   \`\`\`

2. **Gate P1: ESLint (BLOCKER)**
   Use \`mcp__eslint__lint-files\` on modified files
   - If errors → Fix immediately before continuing
   - If warnings → Document, continue

3. **Gate P2: Context7 (IF new library)**
   If you're using a library for the first time:
   - Use \`mcp__context7__resolve-library-id\` → get library ID
   - Use \`mcp__context7__get-library-docs\` → get latest docs
   - Don't guess API usage, get authoritative docs

4. **Gate P3: Memory Update (VERIFICATION)**
   If you made significant decision:
   - Call /update-memory with WHY (not just WHAT)
   - Document trade-offs, alternatives, validation

## Critical Rules

**From ORCHESTRATION.md ${agent.name} section:**
${getAgentCriticalRules(agent.name, ORCHESTRATION)}

## Success Criteria

**Definition of Done:**
- ✅ All assigned tasks completed (T${agent.tasks.start}-T${agent.tasks.end})
- ✅ Build passes (pnpm build → exit 0)
- ✅ ESLint clean (no errors)
- ✅ Tests pass (pnpm test)
- ✅ Périmètres respected (no forbidden file writes)

## Error Handling

**3-Strike Rule:**
- Strike 1: Analyze + attempt fix + retry
- Strike 2: Document in memory + alternative approach + retry
- Strike 3: ESCALATE TO HUMAN (create GitHub Issue + STOP)

**Rollback:**
If critical error breaks build:
\`\`\`bash
git revert [last-commit]
/update-memory "Rolled back [feature] due to [error]"
\`\`\`

## Execution

Read context files above → Implement tasks → Run checkpoints → Document decisions → Report completion.

**GO!** 🚀
  `;

  // 3. Launch agent via Task tool
  const startTime = Date.now();

  await launchAgent({
    subagent_type: agent.name,
    description: `Execute ${agent.name} implementation`,
    prompt: agentPrompt
  });

  const endTime = Date.now();
  const durationS = Math.round((endTime - startTime) / 1000);

  // 4. Run checkpoints
  await runCheckpoints(agent.name, agent.allowed);

  // 5. Log agent end
  pulse.logEnd(agent.name, {
    duration_s: durationS,
    tasks_completed: `T${agent.tasks.start}-T${agent.tasks.end}`,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  });

  console.log(`✅ ${agent.name} completed (${durationS}s)`);
}

// Helper: Run checkpoints
async function runCheckpoints(agentName, allowedDirs) {
  console.log(`\n🔍 Running checkpoints for ${agentName}...`);

  // Checkpoint 1: Build (P0 BLOCKER)
  console.log('Gate P0: Build Check...');
  const buildResult = await runBash('pnpm build');

  if (buildResult.exitCode !== 0) {
    pulse.logCheckpoint('build', 'fail', {
      agent: agentName,
      exit_code: buildResult.exitCode,
      error: buildResult.stderr
    });
    throw new Error(`Build failed for ${agentName}. BLOCKING.`);
  }

  pulse.logCheckpoint('build', 'pass', {
    agent: agentName,
    exit_code: 0,
    duration_ms: buildResult.duration
  });

  // Checkpoint 2: ESLint (P1 BLOCKER)
  console.log('Gate P1: ESLint Check...');

  // Get files modified by agent (in allowed dirs)
  const modifiedFiles = await getModifiedFiles(allowedDirs);

  if (modifiedFiles.length > 0) {
    const lintResult = await mcpEslintLintFiles(modifiedFiles);

    if (lintResult.errors > 0) {
      pulse.logCheckpoint('lint', 'fail', {
        agent: agentName,
        errors: lintResult.errors,
        files: modifiedFiles.length
      });
      throw new Error(`ESLint errors detected for ${agentName}. BLOCKING.`);
    }

    pulse.logCheckpoint('lint', 'pass', {
      agent: agentName,
      errors: 0,
      warnings: lintResult.warnings,
      files: modifiedFiles.length
    });
  } else {
    pulse.logCheckpoint('lint', 'skip', {
      agent: agentName,
      reason: 'no_files_modified'
    });
  }

  // Checkpoint 3: Tests (P2 VERIFICATION)
  console.log('Gate P2: Test Check...');
  const testResult = await runBash('pnpm test');

  if (testResult.exitCode !== 0) {
    pulse.logCheckpoint('test', 'fail', {
      agent: agentName,
      exit_code: testResult.exitCode
    });
    console.warn(`⚠️  Tests failed for ${agentName} (non-blocking, document)`);
  } else {
    pulse.logCheckpoint('test', 'pass', {
      agent: agentName,
      exit_code: 0
    });
  }

  console.log(`✅ Checkpoints complete for ${agentName}\n`);
}
```

**Agent Execution Order (Sequential V6 MVP):**
1. backend-specialist (foundation layer)
2. frontend-specialist (UI layer)
3. testing-specialist (validation layer)
4. devops-specialist (if present - deployment layer)

**Between agents:** Wait for completion + checkpoints before starting next.

